  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Detyens Shipyards has $242M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Detyens Shipyards has 21 awards this fiscal year, and the average award size is $11.5M. Detyens Shipyards' obligations are up 1.3% year over year. Detyens Shipyards received the majority of FY2026 obligations from the Department of Defense, which obligated $193M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $41.6M and the Department of Commerce with $7.2M. Detyens Shipyards' multiyear pattern shows obligations of $96.5M in FY21, $143M in FY22, $91.7M in FY23, $121M in FY24, $239M in FY25, and $242M in FY26. Detyens Shipyards' current-year totals are partial, covering fiscal year to date, and the headline figures are contract obligations except award-value figures in specific award tables. This snapshot helps contractors and partners see scale, customer concentration, and recent momentum in Detyens Shipyards' federal work.",
